WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
A jar of white crystals.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.200
The label has fallen off.

3
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.760
It could be one of many salts, and
plenty of them look just like it.

4
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.400
Chemists look for one clear sign: a gas,

5
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.300
a solid of a telltale shade,
a flame of a telltale shade.

6
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.700
So how can a few test tubes
reveal exactly which salt it is?

7
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.640
In this mission, you'll learn
what makes a good test,

8
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.620
and how to record what you see precisely.

9
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:31.540
Then you'll find out why one
test needs acid added first,

10
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.260
and why the wrong acid would spoil it.

11
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.630
Your mission: find out how a few test tubes
can name the salt in an unlabelled jar.